From: Devin (resumed session artistic-pleasure)
Subject: evals phase 1 — no_prime A/B lever + per-turn metrics capture

backend/realtime_provider.py
  attach token totals + duration to response_completed so the scenario
  runner can diff per-turn usage (totals are cumulative per provider
  session; runner resets its baseline on reconnect).

pwa_server.py
  ?no_prime=1 ws param skips session-start prime AND the provider-reconnect
  re-prime — both injection sites must honor it or the off-arm is
  contaminated by mid-run Gemini reconnects (leak found on review of
  pwa_server.py:729-732).

scripts/scenario-live.py
  --param K=V merges extra ws params after scenario params; per-turn
  in/out tokens + response latency are recorded into turn_log and a
  run-level "totals" block in --events-json.

scripts/scenario-report.py
  tool_calls / in_tokens / out_tokens roll up into report meta so
  ada-ha-scenario-reports docs carry the bench numbers.
